&lt;p&gt;Applies to BL702, BL704 and BL706&lt;br&gt;
Size: 1Kbit&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;eFuse is one time programmable memory. It&amp;rsquo;s mostly used to store things like MAC Address, encryption keys and all other stuff, which are not possible to change after it being burned into eFuse.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In case of BL70X eFuse, once you burn the bit in eFuse, it&amp;rsquo;s not possible to revert it. You can also write/read lock of specific eFuse slots/areas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The structure of the eFuse is available in &lt;a
 class="gdoc-markdown__link"
 href="https://github.com/bouffalolab/bl_mcu_sdk/blob/master/drivers/bl702_driver/regs/ef_data_0_reg.h"
&gt;Bouffalo&amp;rsquo;s SDK&lt;/a&gt; and bfl_mcu_tools (file &lt;code&gt;efuse_cfg_keys.py&lt;/code&gt;), although, it doesn&amp;rsquo;t contains &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt; properties.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Errata</title><link>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl70x/errata/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl70x/errata/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applies to BL702, BL704 and BL706&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="issues-with-running-image-loaded-by-bootrom"
 &gt;
 Issues with running image loaded by BootROM
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl70x/errata/#issues-with-running-image-loaded-by-bootrom" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Issues with running image loaded by BootROM" aria-label="Anchor to: Issues with running image loaded by BootROM" href="#issues-with-running-image-loaded-by-bootrom"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For some reason, &lt;code&gt;BOOTROM_RUN_IMAGE&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;0x1A&lt;/code&gt;) command in BootROM, doesn&amp;rsquo;t work properly, and because of it,
eflash_loader have issues with initializing USB (so sometimes in Windows, the UART driver freeze, so it can&amp;rsquo;t communicate with eflash_loader).
(NOTE: This is observation, other issues are not known yet)&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>